.env
# `/vendor/*`, not `/vendor/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY
# is excluded, and vendor/.htaccess must ship. On a deployment whose DocumentRoot
# is the project root — the misconfiguration that produced a site-wide 403 here —
# vendor/ is inside the web root, and it is the largest attack surface in the tree
# (every dependency's tests, fixtures and dev scripts). Composer does not remove
# unrecognised files, so the deny survives `composer install`.
/vendor/*
!/vendor/.htaccess
# Twig writes compiled templates into HASHED SUBDIRECTORIES (twig/fb/fb02….php), which
# `twig/*.php` does not match — so the cache surfaced as untracked the first time a page
# was rendered outside the test harness. The whole directory is derived.
var/cache/
var/data/
public/assets/vendor/*.map
var/logs/
# Screenshots and other throwaway artefacts written under var/ by tooling. `var/`
# is the project's scratch directory, and 6.8MB of PNGs got committed from a
# verification run because only its named subdirectories were ignored.
#
# A glob rather than another named line: the last two verification runs each invented
# the next number, and `var/shots3/` turned up untracked for exactly the reason the
# paragraph above already describes.
var/shots*/
var/tmp/
# Nominee voice recordings. These are people talking about themselves — the most personal
# thing this platform stores — and a verification run left forty of them untracked in the
# working tree. They belong on the server that received them and nowhere else.
var/uploads/
# Build/deploy archives written here for hand-off. They are outputs of the tree,
# so committing them puts a copy of the tree inside the tree — the first attempt
# produced a 26MB "changed files" zip containing the full-app zip.
var/deploy/

# Off-host build output + user uploads (not committed)
public/assets/dist/
# `public/uploads/*`, not `public/uploads/` — git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory form made the negation below
# impossible. That is why public/uploads/.htaccess — the "Layer 2" the root
# .htaccess has always pointed at — did not exist in any deployment: it could not
# be committed. The uploaded files themselves stay ignored.
public/uploads/*
!public/uploads/.htaccess

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local Composer binary (tool, not project code)
composer.phar

# PHPUnit cache
.phpunit.cache/

# Node modules — only the browser QA tools in tools/browser and tools/qa need
# these, and they are installed on demand (npm i --no-save playwright). Nothing
# the application serves comes from here, and Chromium already ships with the
# environment at /opt/pw-browsers.
/node_modules/
package-lock.json
var/cache/ticket-art/

# Any local .env variant — a moved-aside copy of a real .env still carries the
# real keys, and `git add -A` does not know the difference.
.env.*
!.env.example
